=== RUN   TestGoldensAssertionFiresOnAWriteTurnedRefusal
    contract_test.go:87: REQUIREMENT I check SEEN RED (write became a refusal):
        contract: REQUIREMENT I FAILED — 1 append golden(s) record an outcome nobody expects.
        A write that became a REFUSAL is the pre-R4 signature: CCC_PARITY_CAPTURE=1 rewrites every golden from the live tree, so a capture from before R4 (55c1b998) freezes a blocked append and its unwritten bytes into the reference as contract, and the parity suite then goes green against a frozen defect.
        A refusal that became a WRITE is the opposite failure and is worse: a guard stopped guarding and the reference now certifies that.
        Establish which side is stale before re-capturing — run `go test ./internal/mcpserver -run TestReadPutParity` against the pinned engine. If it passes, the goldens describe current behaviour and it is this table that needs the edit, with the reason written down.
          basic/p-append recorded refused, expected wrote
              golden text: "put: registry splice refused: guard_required (recovery=fix)"
