    scriptdomaintag_u17b_test.go:103: MEASURED row 2 (new host + old engine): REFUSED by name —
        ERROR: script: the arm published an armed-set digest that does not name its domain — refusing with nothing written.
          expected prefix: "armed-set-path-edit:"
          this engine published: "sha256:0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"
          CCC_MRD_BIN=
        An untagged digest is the PATH-BLIND one: it hashes the armed edit PAYLOADS and not the armed SET, so two sets writing identical edits to DIFFERENT files hash the same and the guard admits a splice on a file this host never gated. That is R4 and R5, alive — and it passes silently, because both children of an old engine agree with each other
          → rebuild `mrd` from a meridian-rs tree carrying 14c04a52 and re-declare CCC_MRD_BIN (recovery: env)
